        <briefdescription>
<para>Tests whether a grid cell falls within a line-wise selection. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> for every cell on every row between <computeroutput>anchor.y</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>end.y</computeroutput> (inclusive), regardless of column. This matches Vim <computeroutput>V</computeroutput> line-wise visual mode, where entire lines are selected.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>col</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Column index of the cell to test (0-based). Unused. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>row</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Row index of the cell to test (0-based). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if <computeroutput>row</computeroutput> is within the selected row range.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The row range is normalised internally so dragging upward works. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
