    <briefdescription>
<para>Anchor + end grid-coordinate pair for terminal text selection. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Stores the selection as two <computeroutput>juce::Point&lt;int&gt;</computeroutput> values in grid space. The struct is intentionally minimal — it carries no state beyond the two endpoints and performs no allocation.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Thread context</title><para><bold>MESSAGE THREAD</bold> — created and mutated on the message thread in response to mouse events. A const pointer is passed to <computeroutput>Screen::setText()</computeroutput> and read during <computeroutput>render()</computeroutput> on the same thread.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>Screen::setText() </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
